IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ssa-payments-formulas`

-- Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), point 1064-E10, Table G-2, points 1067G-F28, F31(b) -- worked cases for ssa-payments-formulas.l4.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were worked by hand from the
-- sidecar formulas before running. The facts are those of ssa-cases-payments.l4 (illustrative maximum rates, free areas and limits;
-- the scenarios give no income or asset figures), repeated here because a case file cannot import another case file. The only
-- change is that the two reduction rates are now the Act's.

`Graham` MEANS Senior WITH
    `is male` IS TRUE
    `born on` IS 19700502
    `has 10 years qualifying residence` IS TRUE
    `has a qualifying residence exemption` IS FALSE
    `was receiving a widow or partner payment before pension age` IS FALSE

`Jake` MEANS Senior WITH
    `is male` IS TRUE
    `born on` IS 20060830
    `has 10 years qualifying residence` IS TRUE
    `has a qualifying residence exemption` IS FALSE
    `was receiving a widow or partner payment before pension age` IS FALSE

-- As in ssa-cases-payments.l4, with the first pass's supplied couple rates (25c, 3.9c) left in: the module replaces them.
`Graham's means` MEANS Means WITH
    `maximum payment rate per year` IS 15000
    `ordinary income per year` IS 20000
    `ordinary income free area` IS 1820
    `income reduction per dollar of excess` IS 0.25
    `value of assets` IS 700000
    `assets value limit` IS 187500
    `assets reduction per dollar of excess` IS 0.039

`Jake's means` MEANS Means WITH
    `maximum payment rate per year` IS 20000
    `ordinary income per year` IS 10000
    `ordinary income free area` IS 2080
    `income reduction per dollar of excess` IS 0.5
    `value of assets` IS 300000
    `assets value limit` IS 450000
    `assets reduction per dollar of excess` IS 0.078

`a single homeowner just over the limit` MEANS Means WITH
    `maximum payment rate per year` IS 20000
    `ordinary income per year` IS 0
    `ordinary income free area` IS 2080
    `income reduction per dollar of excess` IS 0
    `value of assets` IS 250999
    `assets value limit` IS 250000
    `assets reduction per dollar of excess` IS 0

§ `point 1064-E10, Table G-2 -- the age pension tapers`

#ASSERT `the Act's income reduction per dollar of excess` EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the Act's assets reduction per dollar of excess` EQUALS 0.078

-- Graham's 50/50 share of income, $20,000, less the $1,820 free area: $18,180 x 0.5 = $9,090 off $15,000, so $5,910. (On the
-- first pass's supplied 25c it would have been $10,455: a finding, see NOTES.md.)
#ASSERT `the income reduced rate under the Act's taper` `Graham's means` EQUALS 5910
-- His assets excess, $512,500 x 19.5 / 250 = $39,975, more than the whole $15,000: nil.
#ASSERT `the assets reduced rate under the Act's taper` `Graham's means` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the provisional annual payment rate under the Act's tapers` `Graham's means` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `an age pension is payable under the Act's tapers` `Graham` 20370502 `Graham's means`

-- Jake: $20,000 - ($10,000 - $2,080) x 0.5 = $16,040, assets under the limit: $16,040, as the first pass has it.
#ASSERT `the provisional annual payment rate under the Act's tapers` `Jake's means` EQUALS 16040
#ASSERT `an age pension is payable under the Act's tapers` `Jake` 20730830 `Jake's means`

-- $999 over the limit is an excess of $750 (multiples of $250): $750 x 19.5 / 250 = $58.50 a year off $20,000. The supplied zero
-- rates in the fixture are ignored.
#ASSERT `the provisional annual payment rate under the Act's tapers` `a single homeowner just over the limit` EQUALS 19941.5

§ `points 1067G-F28, F31(b) -- parental income in common`

-- Excess $95,000 ($150,000 less the $55,000 free area): ($95,000 / 130) x ($450 / $700) = $469.78, to the nearest 10 cents $469.80.
#ASSERT `the F28 result` 150000 0 55000 450 700 EQUALS 469.8
-- A sister who is an FTB child, the parent's FTB maximum rate for her $6,570 a year: 14/365 of it is $252, total $702.
#ASSERT `the F28 total with a relevant sibling` 450 6570 0 EQUALS 702
-- ($95,000 / 130) x ($450 / $702) = $468.44, so $468.40, through the first pass's own rule.
#ASSERT `the parental income test result with F28 computed` 150000 0 55000 FALSE TRUE 450 702 EQUALS 468.4
-- Without parental income in common the F27 branch is unchanged: $95,000 / 130 = $730.77, so $730.80.
#ASSERT `the parental income test result with F28 computed` 150000 0 55000 FALSE FALSE 450 702 EQUALS 730.8
-- Below the free area: nil.
#ASSERT `the parental income test result with F28 computed` 50000 0 55000 FALSE TRUE 450 702 EQUALS 0
